{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you","id":252750,"title":"Scion fans! All of you-","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-08T16:30:23-07:00","id":252750,"title":"Scion fans! All of you-","content":"Which is really what I want to make mention of here: people who post here are all Scion fans or are curious about the game and might become fans. Please remember that common ground when posting.<br /> <br /> Scion is the kind of game that people come to and get involved with from a lot of different directions. This is a good thing.<br /> <br /> Scion is the kind of game that people can and do play in different ways. This also is a good thing.<br /> <br /> Scion is the kind of game that people of different backgrounds and interests in mythology, from loving the Thor and Hercules movies all the way to folks with advanced degrees in mythology and religion, can enjoy. This is also also a good thing.<br /> <br /> Scion is just that big in scope and theme and possibility. And when you hold it in your hands (book or tablet), Scion is yours. We provide the framework in the form of a game book, it is you who decide how to play with, expand, or focus on one small aspect of, what we provide - depending on the games you want to play or stories you want to tell.<br /> <br /> So with all that in mind, please consider how you respond to other Scion fans' posts. A post that says the poster has found new info on how the ancient Scandinavians worshiped a different aspect of Thor is not a threat to you if in your Scion you have been using the Marvel movie version of Asgard. A poster who loves the idea of a version of Scion where you play the children of cereal mascots is not going to force your by-the-book Scion game to change. You are not defending a pure Scion, or a more expansive Scion, or any kind of Scion that you prefer, because Scion does not need to be defended. All you are doing is making another Scion fan feel bad by hammering away at their ideas.<br /> <br /> So, we're all done with that sort of posting.<br /> <br /> From here on in, the moderators will be looking with a jaundiced eye at posts that run counter to the original intent of the thread, and handing out thread suspensions if they determine that you have thread-crapped: basically, if you posted counter to that intention. And all the other rules of the Onyx Path forums still apply as well.<br /> <br /> Additionally, we suggest that if you are starting a new thread that you write a bit at the beginning what your intention with the thread is so that the mods have a better chance of keeping the posts on target. Doesn't have to be a manifesto, it could be as simple as &quot; In-depth analysis of Trickster myths. PHD not required, but would help.&quot;, &quot;Having fun with new powers for Greek Gods, not trying to emulate real myths&quot;, &quot;The Transformers as Scions. I want to explore a totally different rule-set and setting variant&quot;. If you read one of those intention blurbs and grow incensed with white-hot fury, do not post in there because you won't be helping.<br /> <br /> This forum and its posters, here and at WW, have kept Scion alive for years and years, and we at Onyx Path appreciate that more than you can know. We don't want to perma-ban anyone who helped get us here with their love and enthusiasm for Scion. Now, it's time to make sure this forum is a place where Scion fans can freely post their ideas, all of them, and by doing that you will help us grow this new edition.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T18:04:30-07:00","id":252810,"title":"","content":"Ok . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:02:28-07:00","id":252873,"title":"","content":"You're declaring Martial Law?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:14:29-07:00","id":252878,"title":"","content":"I'm asking that you treat each other like the awesome Scion fans you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:27:22-07:00","id":252888,"title":"","content":"I'm not very comfortable with this change. It seems like you guys have good intentions behind it, but people are naturally going to disagree with each other. This makes me frightened to disagree with anyone because it might be considered thread-crapping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:31:32-07:00","id":252890,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between disagreeing and bludgeoning other posters. This forum has had too much of the latter, lately. I have no doubt you'll be OK if you are interested in interesting civil discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:36:47-07:00","id":252894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you#post252750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Marvel movie version of Asgard. A poster who loves the idea of a version of Scion where you play the children of cereal mascots</div> </div> </div> </div>*shudders violently*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you#post252750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From here on in, the moderators will be looking with a jaundiced eye at posts that run counter to the original intent of the thread, and handing out thread suspensions if they determine that you have thread-crapped: basically, if you posted counter to that intention. And all the other rules of the Onyx Path forums still apply as well.<br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>All this suggests is disagreements are now no longer a thing, and that's a very concerning thing in a forum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:48:23-07:00","id":252896,"title":"","content":"See the part where you &quot;shuddered violently&quot;? Don't do that. That's not disagreeing, that's saying that that idea is so appalling to you that can't control your reaction of disgust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T19:57:50-07:00","id":252900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=252896#post252896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the part where you &quot;shuddered violently&quot;? Don't do that. That's not disagreeing, that's saying that that idea is so appalling to you that can't control your reaction of disgust.</div> </div> </div> </div>And at the same time, it's an opinion over a hypothetical you threw out. If we're no longer allowed to have our personal opinions over a game, which you've stated, is very dear to us, that's not a healthy forum environment too.<br /> <br /> edit: And it's a shudder because the idea bothers me. I'm allowed to be bothered by something without condemning the idea itself. It's like Blood Pudding. My relatives love it. I think it's terrifying. As long as it's not shoved down my throat, I don't care what they do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 09-08-2014, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T20:04:53-07:00","id":252903,"title":"","content":"&quot;This idea is not to my liking&quot; or words to that effect, as opposed to a description of involuntary disgust. The former way of expressing your opinion does so without attacking. Can you not see how the latter would be offensive to a poster trying to express their ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T20:12:00-07:00","id":252909,"title":"","content":"I want to be snarky, with a reminder that folks simply saying 'this isn't my cup of tea' also provoking flame wars on this forum but I can see the spirit of what you're trying to accomplish.<br /> <br /> ...it's just worded in a way that suggests we're going to have to be concerned about thoughtcrime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T20:24:32-07:00","id":252931,"title":"","content":"Don't attack and be decent to each other, and that shouldn't be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","user":"RichT","date":".  Edited to remove joke on harsh puishment referring to thoughtcrime and 1984/V for Vendetta but which could be read as a serious reference to real-world evils. 09-09-2014, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T20:45:27-07:00","id":252942,"title":"","content":"I am concerned that the vague declaration in the opening post leaves too much open to interpretation. Could you give us more detailed information on when dissenting opinions will be punished?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T20:56:17-07:00","id":252951,"title":"","content":"There is a very big difference between personal attacks against other posters and criticism of ideas.<br /> <br /> The Native American Pantheon thread was a fairly contentious discussion, but it didn't get personal. There was no name-calling or insulting. There was, however, strident disagreement with how the original poster was suggesting such an issue be handled. If that kind of discussion isn't welcome, I think that's quite a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Scion, as a game, is more problematic than not. It touches a <i>ton</i> of hot-button issues for many, many people. Religion, history, colonialism, imperialism, syncretism, just to name a few. The perspectives on cultures outside of the Western mainstream is very touchy because <i>all</i> portrayals of those cultures in mainstream media are touchy. There's such a huge history of them being done badly. And yes, I hold Scion's first edition as part of that 'done badly' element. It was extremely poor in its representation of several subjects. Let us not forget that the enemies of the Egyptian Pantheon were suicide bomber angels that served a false God. And that's a fairly mainstream culture!<br /> <br /> When you get into the treatment of places like Africa, South America, North America, Australia and Oceania... well, that's just a sticky subject. Perfectly well meaning people can be absolutely insensitive to the issues surrounding those cultures because they just don't know better. That isn't insulting them. It's hard to be aware of those issues, since <i>lack</i> of awareness <b>is</b>one of the issues! <br /> <br /> So if this rule is in place, and someone starts a thread about how they want to see a Mayincatec Pantheon that represents South America... no one is allowed to point out how incredibly offensive that is to every culture involved? No one can offer resources to educate the posters, to make it a more respectful, representative and well rounded idea? Cause if that's where this is going, that's Laaaaaame.<br /> <br /> I don't care if someone plays to play cereal mascots, or use superheroes. That's their gig. If someone wants to say that they'd like help converting the HP Lovecraft Elder Gods into a Mayan Pantheon.. um, I'd have a few things to say about that. And being able to say them seems fairly important to open discussion, even if it hurts some feelings. <br /> <br /> <br /> There is a very big difference between personal attacks against other posters and criticism of ideas.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T21:06:10-07:00","id":252956,"title":"","content":"That is an extremely well written post, and expresses some of my concerns far more eloquently than I could. Thank you, sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T21:24:07-07:00","id":252971,"title":"","content":"While I respect the intent of the devs and mods to create a more welcoming forum environment, I am somewhat concerned by this. I can only hope that this forum is a small enough community, and the mods are active enough, that this truly can be applied on a case-by-case basis. I would also greatly appreciate it if mods continue to provide warnings if they feel a thread is approaching an unacceptable level, so that the posters in question can either make their case as to why their ideas are important and relevant, or tone things down without being banned. I've seen this done well in the past, and hope that it continues to be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T23:40:22-07:00","id":253070,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T23:43:33-07:00","id":253072,"title":"","content":"Thank's for adressing an issue that I've felt has been on the rise for a while. While the it might be a harsh measure, I hope it will work to calm things down and allow more free discussion than previously. Hopefully, the forum will take a turn for the better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T01:02:02-07:00","id":253148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253072#post253072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank's for adressing an issue that I've felt has been on the rise for a while. While the it might be a harsh measure, I hope it will work to calm things down and allow more free discussion than previously. Hopefully, the forum will take a turn for the better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How is it going to allow more free discussion if dissenting opinions can be flagged for threadcrapping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T01:55:01-07:00","id":253160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253148#post253148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it going to allow more free discussion if dissenting opinions can be flagged for threadcrapping?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because threadcrapping is not conducive to a free discussion. Hence trying to avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:28:37-07:00","id":253168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253160#post253160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because threadcrapping is not conducive to a free discussion. Hence trying to avoid it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only the most extreme examples of threadcrapping are definitely threadcrapping though, and that has been against the rules for a while. They are talking about sliding the bar upwards, into the territory where a reasonable objection could be mistaken for threadcrapping because it's not phrased in a political correct manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:32:12-07:00","id":253171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253148#post253148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it going to allow more free discussion if dissenting opinions can be flagged for threadcrapping?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly believe you are overinterprenting the original statement of RichT <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What he's asking for, is more politness and less thread derailing coupled with positive critique. It's not really about &quot;dissenting&quot; opinion as much as it's about actually being polite and answering a thread in a manmer that is constructive rather than destructive.<br /> <br /> As an example: I ask &quot;Does anyone have any suggestions for a story were Tor and Zeus are the same god?&quot; I believe it would be okay to say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Historically, they weren't the same god so I believe this is a bad idea&quot; </div> </div> </div>...as long as you actually add something else to the discussion without derailing the thread from its original intent. Such as:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Historically, they weren't the same god so I believe this is a bad idea, However, if you intend on doing it, it might be a good idea to bring up why Toreuz would do this. Perhaps Zeus grew tired of ye old pantheon-heading and decided to create a new more fun society to the north? Maybe the asgardian pantheon is nothing but a veil to cover something up? Perhaps Mj\u00f6lnir is but the first of a new kind of weapon that the gods have developed and are testing via the newer pantheon&quot; </div> </div> </div>...the second reply is far more constructive and if you absolutely feel you can add nothing than &quot;don't do this&quot; to the thread, then post that and then leave it alone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:43:41-07:00","id":253174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253171#post253171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly believe you are overinterprenting the original statement of RichT <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What he's asking for, is more politness and less thread derailing coupled with positive critique. It's not really about &quot;dissenting&quot; opinion as much as it's about actually being polite and answering a thread in a manmer that is constructive rather than destructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that probably is happening, yes. Part of the problem is that the opening post has a dark and threatening tone, which is further supported by terminology like 'jaundiced eye' and 're-education camps'. I can absolutely get behind the idea of encouraging others to be more polite and nice. That definitely needs to happen! But the tone of the opening post is much more &quot;if you are not nice, you will be punished&quot;, which is the opposite message they were intending to deliver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T02:50:34-07:00","id":253176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253174#post253174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that probably is happening, yes. Part of the problem is that the opening post has a dark and threatening tone, which is further supported by terminology like 'jaundiced eye' and 're-education camps'. I can absolutely get behind the idea of encouraging others to be more polite and nice. That definitely needs to happen! But the tone of the opening post is much more &quot;if you are not nice, you will be punished&quot;, which is the opposite message they were intending to deliver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I hardly read his opening post as threatening. I'm actually reading it more as &quot;You're all great fans of the game and It's good that you're passionate about this. However, passions can easily turn into anger so the mods will be more active&quot;.<br /> <br /> also, the re-education camp reas to me as a joke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not as an actual threat. Also:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't want to perma-ban anyone who helped get us here with their love and enthusiasm for Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>...makes it, at least to me, very clear that he's really trying to make this forum a better and more welcoming place<br /> <br /> However, if a lot of people feel that the opening post is threatening rather than encouraging, I believe RichT will understand and possibly rewrite his post ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T03:11:54-07:00","id":253181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253176#post253176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if a lot of people feel that the opening post is threatening rather than encouraging, I believe RichT will understand and possibly rewrite his post ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the best idea. I genuinely think his intent was good, and he wanted to convey a positive message that encourages everyone to be supportive and friendly to their fellow Scion fans. But even joking that people would be put in re-education camps hasn't been okay since 1945.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:10:13-07:00","id":253217,"title":"","content":"My intent is clear: stop bullying each other. If you've never done that, you'll be able to post as you always have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:51:16-07:00","id":253230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253217#post253217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My intent is clear: stop bullying each other. If you've never done that, you'll be able to post as you always have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>I throughly approve of this message!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T05:34:57-07:00","id":253254,"title":"","content":"There are obviously specific posts that led to this. I probably have an idea of which they are, but it would help if we were provided with a few specific examples of big-time no-nos with context from real threads that exist.<br /> <br /> I've seen some people disagree in ways that put people down unintentionally, but I don't see why that's so horrible.<br /> <br /> I feel like this whole thing boils down to, &quot;this is just a game, so don't bring in all this business about cultures being offended.&quot; If that's the case, I don't like the ruling. Mostly because some people don't know they're being offensive. However, if someone recognizes that others may not like the idea, the requirement of putting a disclaimer is one excellent thing to come out of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T05:35:58-07:00","id":253255,"title":"","content":"I also approve this message. Thank you, Rich.<br /> <br /> A big part of the reason why I have never posted on this forum - up until VERY recently - is, quite frankly, I thought there was a lot of bullying flying around. I've been coming to read and watch for information regarding Scion 2e. Engaging with people here has been an intimidating prospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2789-laume78","name":"laume78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:09:00-07:00","id":253303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253254#post253254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this whole thing boils down to, &quot;this is just a game, so don't bring in all this business about cultures being offended.&quot; If that's the case, I don't like the ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what it means. I'll let Rich address the finer points of his post, but as administrator, I should clear up this bit. Racism, religious bigotry, and other group attacks, even within a fictional context, are reportable offenses under Rule 1. While we allow some leeway for the forums to be self-correcting in this area, it's a moderation issue, not one for individual posters, and the rules haven't changed.<br /> <br /> If you've been seeing group attacks and no action has been taken, that's probably either because it's been taken privately (we're reducing, but not eliminating that), or because the post wasn't reported. The mod team can't review every post on the forums, so we rely on the Flag Report feature to spotlight potential problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:14:04-07:00","id":253304,"title":"","content":"A thought to all the people concerned about not being able to &quot;correct&quot; people that are being insensitive to cultural issues:<br /> <br /> <b>It is not your job to do this</b>. You are not a moderator.<br /> <br /> If you think someone is being offensive <i>flag their post</i> and you can include the hows, whys, and that you think it is ignorance instead of purposeful bigotry. Don't break rules (threadcrap) because you think someone else is breaking a rule (posting group attacks with ignorant cultural statements). Either figure out a way to politely enter the thread to express your feelings and not threadcrap, or just report it and let the mods sort it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:41:38-07:00","id":253315,"title":"","content":"...And how exactly is that constructive? Calling a moderator in every time someone posts something with as much cultural sensitivity as a 40's comic book? It's better to toss a warning at them with no explanation of <i>why</i> that topic is sensitive, of <i>why</i> their idea is offensive?<br /> <br /> No one is being a Forum Vigilante, valiantly attacking the mean, mean racists. I haven't even seen anyone (recently) being <i>intentionally</i> racist. We're talking about deep-seated cultural biases that are remarkably hard to deal with. About things like the perception that all Native Americans are the same, but tiny and virtually undocumented groups of Europeans deserve special attention. About the perception of Mayans and Aztecs as virtually identical bloodthirsty savage tribes that sacrificed people willy-nilly like some B-movie horror villain. <br /> <br /> No one deserves to be suspended or reported for that. But they also don't need to continue spreading such ideas. That's when people have stepped in and said &quot;Hey, woah, woah. You're going about this all wrong and it's pretty offensive. Here's why, and how you could do it without the racism!&quot;<br /> <br /> It happens <i>a lot</i> on the Scion forum, because Scion deals with a <i>lot</i> of marginalized, poorly represented groups and periods of history. And no, it is bloody well not reasonable to expect everyone to offer their insight with a smile and polite diction. As long as no personal attacks are involved and no one is insulted, belittled or denigrated, how is that different from any interaction.. uh, ever? <br /> <br /> Scenario 1) &quot;I wanna play with superheroes!&quot; No one is harmed by this, at all. Ever. There is no need to respond if you disagree with the premise.<br /> Scenario 2) &quot;I wanna play with cereal mascots!&quot; No one is harmed by this, at all. Ever. There is no need to respond if you disagree with the premise.<br /> Scenario 3) &quot;I wanna play with HP Lovecraft Gods!&quot; No one is harmed by this, at all. Ever. There is no need to respond if you disagree with the premise.<br /> Scenario 4) &quot;I wanna play with Coyote and Brer Rabbit!&quot; This brings up a bunch of loaded, harmful stereotypes. It needs to be addressed, because <i>not</i> addressing it allows ignorance and casual, passive forms of racism to proliferate. There <i>is</i> a need to respond, <i>especially</i> if you disagree. <br /> <br /> Is the correct response to say &quot;You're an idiot, those are racist!&quot; with no explanation and personal attacks? No. Is the correct response to offer information and explanation as to <i>why</i> those things are racist and insensitive? Yes. That's being a good person who wants to see improvement in the world and in cultural perceptions.<br /> <br /> <br /> It is a very poor choice to change the purpose of a discussion board from &quot;Hey, what does everyone think of this idea?&quot; to &quot;Hey, what does everyone who already agrees with me think of this idea?&quot; <br /> <br /> Personal attacks and bullying have <i>always</i> been things that the moderators and administrators have been on the lookout for. Now they're also going to have the Hurt Feelings Patrol? Getting your feelings hurt because people disagree with you, even dismissively or angrily, is <i>not at all the same</i> as being the target of bullying or personal abuse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:49:47-07:00","id":253317,"title":"","content":"I think maybe I should also point out that I haven't seen a particular problem with people discussing cultural sensitivity issues. The problem posts are much more within Telgar's scenarios 1-3 than 4. Note the examples Rich uses in his post.<br /> <br /> As for scenario 4, please note what I said about &quot;allow[ing] leeway for the forums to be self-correcting.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 09-09-2014, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T08:50:20-07:00","id":253318,"title":"","content":"Wow, guys, what the hell is this?<br /> <br /> I don't want to suggest that what Rich is proposing is hard to do, but the sheer amount of railing against &quot;Don't be a bully&quot; (Or as I would have put it, &quot;Don't be a dick&quot;) and the logic bending to make it seem justified is almost absurd.<br /> <br /> Look, Scion can be a sensitive game. But the heart of it is simple, the same as any other game. It's about human beings coming together and having fun by being human together.<br /> <br /> Rich is asking, and I appreciate it when we do this, that we be excellent human beings. Or, if that sounds daunting, be the sort of person who makes gaming at your table a fun and safe place to be.<br /> <br /> Decency is not too much to ask for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:10:05-07:00","id":253350,"title":"","content":"There's a pretty big difference in tone between what was asked for originally and what is being distilled out of that.<br /> <br /> If the original statement had been &quot;Hey, Scion Fans, you're all lovely people, please don't be dicks to each other!&quot; Well, that's totally fine and should get unconditional, 100% support from everyone who isn't a dick. But that isn't what I, and apparently a lot of other people got out of the original post.<br /> <br /> Here's what's being objected to: &quot;All you are doing is making another Scion fan feel bad by hammering away at their ideas.&quot; and &quot;From here on in, the moderators will be looking with a jaundiced eye at posts that run counter to the original intent of the thread, and handing out thread suspensions if they determine that you have thread-crapped: basically, if you posted counter to that intention.&quot;<br /> <br /> What do I get from that? It certainly isn't &quot;Hey, don't be a dick!&quot; No. It's more like &quot;Hey, don't voice disagreement or dislike for anything!&quot; or maybe &quot;Don't hurt anyone's feelings by telling them their ideas are bad.&quot; That seems like a legitimate thing to get upset about. Especially when the <i>tone of the non-attacking disagreement</i> was specifically called out as objectionable.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253317#post253317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe I should also point out that I haven't seen a particular problem with people discussing cultural sensitivity issues. The problem posts are much more within Telgar's scenarios 1-3 than 4. Note the examples Rich uses in his post.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I can understand that. If it's Scenarios 1-3 that are bringing this post to the forums, sure, that's an issue. However I can't recall any such situations appearing in the last few weeks. What <i>has</i> appeared in the last few weeks are things like the Native American Pantheon thread, the whole Nazis thing, arguments about how evil Gods are.. you know, kinda serious, real-world issue type things. If there were a bunch of really <i>nasty</i> arguments going on in the smaller threads that I missed.. uh, well then I guess I look silly for missing the point of this thread. But I just scanned a bunch pretty fast and don't see any bullying. There <i>has</i> been a recent thread (now deleted) that specifically addressed this issue in a rather antagonistic way, which was also tied directly to the cultural, historical and racial issues noted above. So maybe my misunderstanding of what prompted this new sticky is reasonable?<br /> <br /> If we're talking about &quot;Just please stop being dicks about people wanting to play the game differently from you&quot;, well sure. But it comes off a lot more as &quot;Please don't hurt anyone's feelings no matter what they post.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 09-09-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:15:46-07:00","id":253353,"title":"","content":"I said it earlier, and I'll say it again, but I feel like we need to wait and see how the policy is actually implemented, rather than how it's phrased. Remember that all of us, yes even the mods and devs, are people. We can make mistakes. BUT we also have the capacity to judge things in context. I don't think we've seen enough of the implementation of this new policy to criticize it from a truly informed standpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:23:07-07:00","id":253360,"title":"","content":"See, it looks to me like you people are blowing things out of proportion.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, someone's response to Rich saying it was okay for people to base their Norse gods off the Marvel Universe was to violently shudder(Which, for the record, I doubt he actually did).<br /> <br /> It's stupid to assume they're saying &quot;Don't disagree with each other&quot;, because they have eyes and work with the internet a lot. I think they know that that's not only a bad idea, but it's also <i>impossible</i> to actually do. And quite frankly, they've said <i>several times</i> they actually like constructive disagreement.<br /> <br /> What they are advocating against is blindly and angrily acting against something. They are against people feeling like they did something wrong by doing something silly or different or something purely by mistake, like they did something wrong. If they did, report them! If not, be a decent human being in discussing your concerns! There's no need to trample people.<br /> <br /> So, no, I never once got they were saying don't disagree. They're saying make this a place you would feel comfortable disagreeing in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And quite frankly, if you see someone trying to build something you don't like, leave it alone. Heaven forbid, there have been a number of WoD fangames or new mechanics I thought were stupid as sin that I just ignored. And you know what, that worked!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-09-2014, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:31:07-07:00","id":253366,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, I find it ironic that I'm warned about being put in a re eduction camp if I'm not overly careful of my tone ... isn't the &quot;joke&quot; is the very sort of thing the moderators are trying to halt?<br /> <br /> Don't tell me that my distaste for a comic based take on mythology is on the same level as that, cmon.<br /> <br /> All this is going to do is kill the discussion on the board between people who have dissenting opinions and want to discuss heavier topics. For example, I already know which threads to avoid because if I even peek in there, someone's going to think they're being picked on. <br /> <br /> If we can't tell people that, hey, smashing every similar culture that isn't white European together is the very foundation on what some forms of racism are... because we're going to hurt the posters feelings?<br /> <br /> If the Scion forums become a wasteland (yes, a wasteland, I don't come here for comic characters fighting cereal mascots rules) without any interesting insights on the actual mythology the game was built on, then that's a depressing future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:35:29-07:00","id":253369,"title":"","content":"There's that blowing things out of proportion thing again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:43:08-07:00","id":253374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253360#post253360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, it looks to me like you people are blowing things out of proportion.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, someone's response to Rich saying it was okay for people to base their Norse gods off the Marvel Universe was to violently shudder(Which, for the record, I doubt he actually did).<br /> <br /> It's stupid to assume they're saying &quot;Don't disagree with each other&quot;, because they have eyes and work with the internet a lot. I think they know that that's not only a bad idea, but it's also <i>impossible</i> to actually do. And quite frankly, they've said <i>several times</i> they actually like constructive disagreement.<br /> <br /> What they are advocating against is blindly and angrily acting against something. They are against people feeling like they did something wrong by doing something silly or different or something purely by mistake, like they did something wrong. If they did, report them! If not, be a decent human being in discussing your concerns! There's no need to trample people.<br /> <br /> So, no, I never once got they were saying don't disagree. They're saying make this a place you would feel comfortable disagreeing in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And quite frankly, if you see someone trying to build something you don't like, leave it alone. Heaven forbid, there have been a number of WoD fangames or new mechanics I thought were stupid as sin that I just ignored. And you know what, that worked!</div> </div> </div> </div>I shuddered because taking that mythology and putting the marvelverse in its place bothers me. And yes, I did shudder. Enough that my raid thought something bad happened in game. It's a pet peeve and before you start preaching about ignoring things you don't like. .. actually look at the board? <br /> <br /> I don't go into others threads about their home brew ideas and tell them they're badwrong (unless they're actively trying to push something to be official and it is so hurtful to that culture it gives sympathy pains), but now I have to coddle them when they come into my threads and spout nonsense like Shango being the God of Racism.<br /> <br /> If my dislike of Marvel verse bothers someone on this forum then they're either Disney or a person with a hard core obsession with the movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 09-09-2014, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T09:45:09-07:00","id":253376,"title":"","content":"Edit: the troubles have been in threads that deal with serious issues, not the homebrews. We don't care if you play the game with bugs bunny but don't try to put him on the same pedestal when we're talking about real cultures and their personal stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T10:20:50-07:00","id":253406,"title":"","content":"@Aynie Actually, we are saying that if someone comes to your thread and jams in a bunch of stuff that runs counter to the intent of your thread then they are doing the very thing we are trying to stop. You can report them, or you can explain reasonably why what they are posting is not in sync with your thread: just keep it civil. And if you take the time to post a bit of a lead-in to your initial post that specifies that you are looking at real world cultural issues, then it makes it even easier for the mods to determine who has strayed from the thread's intended purpose.<br /> <br /> And towards civility, I edited my &quot;joke&quot; post because I could see that if someone did not relate what I posted back to the &quot;thoughtcrime&quot; comment that you made, then someone could misinterpret my intent of referencing &quot;1984&quot; or &quot;V for Vendetta&quot;-like fictional situations. My intent was to comment on what I thought must be your joking use of &quot;thoughtcrime&quot; in this situation with an equally jokey and over the top reference to our thought police hauling you away. Sorry for the poor phrasing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T11:22:46-07:00","id":253488,"title":"","content":"I believe it's going to be very common for any disagreement to be called not being &quot;in synch&quot; with a thread. Especially with such recent evidence as the Native American Pantheon thread, where just that was argued many, many times by the original poster and some others. And that leads right back to &quot;No disagreement!&quot; and an attitude of only posting when you support an idea. Sure, it won't hurt anyone's feelings, but it's also a bloody <i>boring</i> and unproductive way to have discussions.<br /> <br /> What if I don't want any pesky, preachy people invading my thread and blabbing <i>on and on</i> about cultural sensitivity and politics and race issues? What if I just want to have <i>fun</i> and tell crazy awesome stories about adventures with whatever makes my group happy? Well, as long as the resulting commentary doesn't contain offensive words, personal attacks or slander against me, <i>that commentary is perfectly on topic</i>. It's not out of synch, it isn't thread-crapping, it isn't bullying and it isn't an attack. Even if it hurts feelings.<br /> <br /> That's my issue. The existing guidelines have always protected against personal attacks, insults and bullying. A new Happy Thoughts Patrol that protects against hurt feelings is just not necessary and is absolutely contrary to constructive discussion.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;It's just a game! Why can't you just let people enjoy it however they want to!&quot; seems to be at the basis of this whole idea.<br /> <br /> For the same reason Feminist Frequency exists. For the same reason people dissect popular media to point out the problems with race, sex, gender identity and socioeconomic status. For the reason reason that Hollywood is subject to criticism when they cast a white actor for a person from an Inuit culture, or stick a random white guy into a movie about another culture just so it'll sell more tickets. Because those are real issues that exist all around the world and just letting people continue on with stereotypes and uninformed wrongness contributes to a culture of ignorance and intolerance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T12:07:20-07:00","id":253527,"title":"","content":"I'm actually amazed about what this thread has become less than two days after the initial posting. That something as simple as this can grow so widely out of proportion.<br /> <br /> Scion, at its heart, is an action game with lots of storytelling potential. If someone wants to use superheroes with the Scion system, make gods dependent on faith from humans, removing or adding pantheons, editing pantheons or rewrite them from scratch its okay. It's after all, a fantasy game made for exploring a different world. For some people, that means 100% accuracy for the source material and keeping the facts straight. For others, that mean letting go of serious issues and flinging oneself into adventure and action.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T12:42:15-07:00","id":253553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253488#post253488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it's going to be very common for any disagreement to be called not being &quot;in synch&quot; with a thread. Especially with such recent evidence as the Native American Pantheon thread, where just that was argued many, many times by the original poster and some others. And that leads right back to &quot;No disagreement!&quot; and an attitude of only posting when you support an idea. Sure, it won't hurt anyone's feelings, but it's also a bloody <i>boring</i> and unproductive way to have discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a serious excluded middle going on here.<br /> <br /> There's a difference between &quot;I disagree with the fundamental premise of this thread,&quot; and, &quot;I disagree with how you're going about implementing your ideas.&quot;<br /> <br /> If I start a thread on wanting to do a Marvel inspired highly pop-culture not super accurate to historical mythology Greek Pantheon, and you just don't like that and don't have anything you want to say besides how much you don't like it? Stay out. It's not that much to ask. It's already a general forum rule as it is. If you disagree with my take on Bacchus, not based on real mythology but the premise I'm working on, go ahead and disagree. You might have a really good idea/point/critique. Those are good disagreements that can creature good discussions.<br /> <br /> If all your suggestions are about how to do things more accurate to mythology though... are you really respecting the point of the thread? If your idea happens to have that side effect that's cool, but that shouldn't be the motivation of your idea. It isn't a selling point of your idea to the premise of the thread. If you keep hammering in on how to make things more like the real mythology, even if the suggestions are otherwise good, it starts to feel like what you're trying to say is really, &quot;play real mythology, not what you said you want.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, as long as the resulting commentary doesn't contain offensive words, personal attacks or slander against me, <i>that commentary is perfectly on topic</i>. It's not out of synch, it isn't thread-crapping, it isn't bullying and it isn't an attack. Even if it hurts feelings. </div> </div> </div>That's just unreasonable. You don't need to use offensive words or make personal attacks to threadcrap. There's a reason why these are separate forum rules. I can make completely on topic posts with offensive words, and be completely nice and civil while crapping all over a thread.<br /> <br /> And what benefit is there to the tone of the forums if we're saying posters to have the right to exercise their ability to hurt other people's feelings <i>on purpose</i> without potential moderation? We're allowed to ignore rule 1 of the forum as long as we think we're fighting a good fight? Why is it so much to ask people to flag posts instead of responding in a fashion they know is going to hurt people's feelings? If the person is saying things that are problems from a social justice perspective, make the case in the report to the mods and let them handle it. What's wrong with that? Why can't the mods be trusted to pull people aside and talk them about how posting culturally insensitive things is problematic and needs to stop?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the same reason Feminist Frequency exists. For the same reason people dissect popular media to point out the problems with race, sex, gender identity and socioeconomic status. For the reason reason that Hollywood is subject to criticism when they cast a white actor for a person from an Inuit culture, or stick a random white guy into a movie about another culture just so it'll sell more tickets. Because those are real issues that exist all around the world and just letting people continue on with stereotypes and uninformed wrongness contributes to a culture of ignorance and intolerance. </div> </div> </div>So make good threads about these topics for people to read. Start threads about how to respect cultures without getting in the primary motivation of sitting down and playing a fun game with fiction and mythology. Fill the forums with awesome threads with lots and lots of material so that people can see why being respectful doesn't have to fall to the side of simplicity and fun. Be the Scion Feminist Frequency that's not sitting around trashing ideas that touch sensitive issues poorly, but actually explaining the issues and talking about how to use those sensitive issues well. If the forums have tons of <i>positive</i> threads about this stuff rather than it only coming up to play whack-a-mole when individual posters decide that a thread has crossed the line of &quot;not my bag I don't care&quot; and into &quot;problematic and needs to be addressed in public discussion,&quot; then we have a lot better of an atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-09-2014, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T13:07:02-07:00","id":253559,"title":"","content":"@Telgar I stated in the original post that our previous forum standards are still in place. Nothing has changed in terms of how the mods are dealing with racism, sexism, etc. However, we do feel that this forum has become a combative and threatening place for fans of Scion who would like to post here, and as far as we can define it, that negative reputation is the result of bullying posting habits by some of the posters already here. Thus, new rules and scrutiny of such behavior. The same process will take place with the mods reviewing any reports or issuing warnings as they have.<br /> <br /> You make a lot of good points about how interconnected mythology and culture are in a game like Scion, and that is something the mods will need to keep in mind. The injustices of the world are definitely important topics and exactly what a &quot;real world&quot; game like Scion gives players a chance to wrestle with in-setting. At the same time, can you understand that some people would prefer not to deal with those issues when talking about their game, though? This does not make them enablers of social injustice in the world because of what they post on these forums, it just makes them fans of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T13:49:24-07:00","id":253565,"title":"","content":"It would help if you defined what you consider to be bullying posting habits. I deal with bullying as a teacher, and it's something very different from rudeness or sass in my frame of reference. I'm genuinely against bullying in all forms, but I'd like to know what is being defined as bullying in this situation and this context. I'm also struggling with the idea that &quot;I just want to play my game and have fun, man! Don't harsh my buzz with all this politics and equality!&quot; is a good reason to suspend someone if they're not being unreasonably aggressive and insulting.<br /> <br /> There are clearly appropriate times and places for different standards.<br /> <br /> When my friends post their vacation photographs on Facebook, I don't launch into a point-by-point criticism of their technical and aesthetic skills. That'd be rude, and it'd be absolutely uncalled for. They're just having fun! They're taking pictures to make a memory and be happy. They don't care about lighting, composition or exposure. It would be silly of me to bring up such issues.<br /> <br /> When a random stranger posts photographs on a photography discussion board, you better believe I dive into a point-by-point criticism of their technical and aesthetic skills. In this case, not only is just pressing &quot;Like&quot; instead of providing feedback unhelpful, it's detrimental to the person posting since they get reinforcement that what they're doing is great, even if it actually needs a great deal of improvement.<br /> <br /> Up until now, this discussion board has allowed for both approaches. Unless there's some kind of labeling system (Happy Face Thread Icon for vacation photos, Frowny Face Thread Icon for technical work?) it seems absolutely silly to say that you have to abide by Facebook rules here on a forum specifically dedicated to discussing the game in question. And especially when the vacation photos can easily end up being on the level of sticking a feathered hat on your heat when you're in Arizona and giving the camera your best version of &quot;Indian Face&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:01:49-07:00","id":253574,"title":"","content":"Please understand a thread ban is not the same thing as a forum ban or suspension. It's a request to stay out of a topic that we'll make if we see someone not participating in a discussion in good faith, attempting to derail a conversation or otherwise posting just to say an idea is bad and not to do it. If someone ignores a threadban then they can expect some disciplinary to be taken, up to and including being banned from the forums in general, which is no different consequence than one would get for ignoring any other moderator directives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 09-09-2014, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:12:22-07:00","id":253579,"title":"","content":"It's also not silly to expect people to abide by the same set of rules of discourse when they apply to everyone equally. If you don't feel that you can express yourself in a civil, non-confrontational manner then this is probably not the forum for you. This is what we want to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:21:23-07:00","id":253585,"title":"","content":"So, here's something I think needs to be said, and it's not the easiest thing to say.<br /> <br /> With regards to cultural respect, we have done wrong. There are things in <i>Scion</i> itself that are pretty bad. The treatment of Mesoamerican pantheons is a good example. That's something we can only really fix with a new edition. Cultural respect in the pantheon descriptions is a big deal to us. It comes up literally every time I have lunch with one of the main writers. (I mean literally literally.)<br /> <br /> We've also allowed some stuff on the forums -- including recently -- that we shouldn't have. In reviewing the last few weeks of threads, I've seen stuff that we should have taken action on, specifically because of racism. We're not here to set out a policy against trying to improve <i>Scion</i>'s cultural respect. Quite the opposite.<br /> <br /> Where politics and equality intersect <i>Scion </i>-- and those are some big intersections -- they're legitimate topics for discussion, and I don't plan to have the moderators crack down on anything related to that that doesn't violate current forum rules. I <i>do</i>, however, intend to make sure that the rules get enforced for <i>Scion</i> as much as they do for, say, cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:27:10-07:00","id":253590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253488#post253488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my issue. The existing guidelines have always protected against personal attacks, insults and bullying. A new Happy Thoughts Patrol that protects against hurt feelings is just not necessary and is absolutely contrary to constructive discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no new patrol being formed. There are no new rules being added. The problem is that even though the existing rules do protect against personal attacks, insults, and bullying, we have had consistent problems with people violating those rules. So, we are going to be keeping a tighter watch for violations of the existing rules. You are still welcome to express disagreement, as long as you do so in a respectful, productive way (ie don't break any of the existing rules).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:28:49-07:00","id":253591,"title":"","content":"I'd still like to know where the line of &quot;bullying&quot; falls. Hurt feelings are very different from intentional harassment and abuse. I'd like to be fully aware of which one is being watched for and what degree of smiling faces is expected before any discussions continue...<br /> <br /> <br /> In fact, it may be reasonable to note that since this post was made, there has been no significant discussion in the forum. Correlation vs causation and all that, true, and this is a fairly slow-paced forum, but still. It's something to note.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253590#post253590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no new patrol being formed. There are no new rules being added. The problem is that even though the existing rules do protect against personal attacks, insults, and bullying, we have had consistent problems with people violating those rules. So, we are going to be keeping a tighter watch for violations of the existing rules. You are still welcome to express disagreement, as long as you do so in a respectful, productive way (ie don't break any of the existing rules).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a much more acceptable way of phrasing things. If that is the entirety of the original intent, then I do not object. The original post and following replies seemed to indicate much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 09-09-2014, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:57:50-07:00","id":253611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253565#post253565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When my friends post their vacation photographs on Facebook, I don't launch into a point-by-point criticism of their technical and aesthetic skills. That'd be rude, and it'd be absolutely uncalled for. They're just having fun! They're taking pictures to make a memory and be happy. They don't care about lighting, composition or exposure. It would be silly of me to bring up such issues.<br /> <br /> When a random stranger posts photographs on a photography discussion board, you better believe I dive into a point-by-point criticism of their technical and aesthetic skills. In this case, not only is just pressing &quot;Like&quot; instead of providing feedback unhelpful, it's detrimental to the person posting since they get reinforcement that what they're doing is great, even if it actually needs a great deal of improvement.<br /> <br /> Up until now, this discussion board has allowed for both approaches. Unless there's some kind of labeling system (Happy Face Thread Icon for vacation photos, Frowny Face Thread Icon for technical work?) it seems absolutely silly to say that you have to abide by Facebook rules here on a forum specifically dedicated to discussing the game in question. And especially when the vacation photos can easily end up being on the level of sticking a feathered hat on your heat when you're in Arizona and giving the camera your best version of &quot;Indian Face&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still falling into a fairly frustrating false dichotomy. There is a huge gap of possible responses to something between, &quot;mindless and contentess likes,&quot; and, &quot;full academic point-by-point cold analysis of all the flaws in something with no eye towards constructive discourse or the poster's feelings.&quot;<br /> <br /> For one thing, you're completely excluding original posters and there stated reasons for <i>why</i> something is being posted. That's why Rich's opening post directly calls on new threads to have their intentions more thoroughly stated. So you can know what kind of responses are contextually appropriate. If the OP clearly wants a &quot;Facebook photo&quot; thread, treat it like that. If they want a, &quot;open season critique anything and everything of my idea,&quot; respond appropriate for that context. If they post, &quot;Hey, I know this picture has a few flaws, but I'm looking for advice on exposure,&quot; don't rant on about composition.<br /> <br /> The default ruthless critique mentality is problematic though. I wouldn't want to be around a photography forum where pictures posted are open season to any and all criticism with zero eye to maintaining some positivity to keep people from getting discouraged. You talk of being a teacher. A teacher should understand that there is a balance with criticism where it shuts people down. People don't like being criticized even if they know they need it. If you create an atmosphere where any posted idea is at constant risk of over-criticism, you discourage people posting things. Who wants to sort through a dozen pages of harsh criticism for a few possible useful ideas?<br /> <br /> And you still haven't said why flagging a racist post and letting the mods handle it is not a functional solution to the &quot;Indian Face&quot; photo if that's what someone posts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:06:01-07:00","id":253651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253591#post253591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd still like to know where the line of &amp;quot;bullying&amp;quot; falls. Hurt feelings are very different from intentional harassment and abuse. I'd like to be fully aware of which one is being watched for and what degree of smiling faces is expected before any discussions continue...<br /> <br /> In fact, it may be reasonable to note that since this post was made, there has been no significant discussion in the forum. Correlation vs causation and all that, true, and this is a fairly slow-paced forum, but still. It's something to note.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a much more acceptable way of phrasing things. If that is the entirety of the original intent, then I do not object. The original post and following replies seemed to indicate much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great to hear! Hoping now that you get where we are coming from that we can all work together to make this both an interesting and welcoming forum for all Scion fans. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T19:34:53-07:00","id":253768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253565#post253565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would help if you defined what you consider to be bullying posting habits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember a year and a half ago, when Eldagusto suggested that a modern take on <i>Journey to the West</i> could take inspiration from the works of Akira Toriyama, and the members of the Scion forum were so offended by this that they raided the Exalted forum to <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/53\" target=\"_blank\">harass Eldagusto and derail his threads</a>?<br /> <br /> <i>Don't do that.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T19:42:05-07:00","id":253771,"title":"","content":"From my perspective, what RichT is asking is not for people to be unable to express their ideas and disagreement with others ideas, but that if you choose to do so, do so by providing constructive criticism rather than straight on aggression.<br /> <br /> Taking the fictional quote &quot;Zeus is the son of Thor and Hera&quot; as an example, I could break this down into 4 general methods of reply that each produce a vastly different feel.<br /> <br /> 1) Positive Specific: &quot;Although I know what you suggest is not how the actual mythology is written, having Zeus as their son opens up a lot of interesting options especially if Loki is now his step-brother.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Positive General: &quot;Your idea seems pretty cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) Negative Specific: &quot;I find that your proposed option of having Zeus as the son of Thor and Hera is a bit strange. Part of the whole charm of Zeus is having him be the father of the Olympian gods rather than mixed in with the rest.&quot;<br /> <br /> 4) Negative General: &quot;Your idea sucks&quot;<br /> <br /> If we look at these different examples, the first 3 can contribute to a fully valid discussion even if the negative specific doesn't come across as rainbows and sunshine. The difference between Negative Specific and Negative General, is the Negative Specific is challenging the idea and following it up with a logical argument while the Negative General statement is a direct attack on the poster rather than the idea.<br /> <br /> In summary, what RichT is asking is to play nice and challenge ideas as they are posted in a constructive manner rather than attack the poster itself. With Scion especially, arguments can be extremely heated and once a thread has devolved into direct attacks against a person, there is no longer any meaningful discussion to be had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T19:46:04-07:00","id":253773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253768#post253768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember a year and a half ago, when Eldagusto suggested that a modern take on <i>Journey to the West</i> could take inspiration from the works of Akira Toriyama, and the members of the Scion forum were so offended by this that they raided the Exalted forum to <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/53\" target=\"_blank\">harass Eldagusto and derail his threads</a>?<br /> <br /> <i>Don't do that.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I remember that event quite differently, actually. Being one of the people Eldagusto decided to make personal attacks against in the &quot;secrecy&quot; of the Exalted forum when he was disagreed with.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You'll notice that I was contributing to the specific discussion involved on that thread, down at the bottom of your link. I'm talking quite politely with Plague of Hats about the exact topic of the thread. While Eldagusto was making personal attacks directed at me. So, yeah, I do remember that pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 09-09-2014, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T20:48:42-07:00","id":253790,"title":"","content":"Little context for thought food. Unfortunately it brings up Atlantis and Yankee Pantheons.<br /> <br /> I may be wrong on this, but I think by and large I've been, and still am, a fairly respected person on White Wolf/Onyx Path forums generally. Granted I have a greater presence in the Off-Topic and nWoD threads than I do Scion, but I've been under the impression I've been reasonablly well liked and reasonably well listened to for a long time now. I'm not a hundred percent I deserve it, but I have had it for a while now.<br /> <br /> And yet, back on the White Wolf forums, even after I got this sort of air of respect, and even having some conversations that indicated that in Scion, I <i>still </i>had people get pretty aggressive with me over the fact I liked the Atlantis And Yankee Pantheons and that I felt like certain arguments(Like the Culture Hero's shouldn't be gods thing) just didn't hold up with the themes of Scion. It was hackle-raising, let me tell you.<br /> <br /> That's with someone who people had at least heard of and had a modicrum respect on a topic that was at least created by White Wolf and therefore had a measure of credit if for no other reason than name attachment.<br /> <br /> Heaven forbid someone completely new come in and put forth ideas that don't have the same backing.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I saw what Rich was talking about, and I also knew where he was going. And yeah, that's my story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T21:17:40-07:00","id":253800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253768#post253768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember a year and a half ago, when Eldagusto suggested that a modern take on <i>Journey to the West</i> could take inspiration from the works of Akira Toriyama, and the members of the Scion forum were so offended by this that they raided the Exalted forum to <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/53\" target=\"_blank\">harass Eldagusto and derail his threads</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember respectfully disagreeing with Eldagusto and his Akira Toriyama idea, along with several other posters, and then discovering that he had gone over to the Exalted forums and made a personal attack thread. He publically called out several people for being terrible and intolerant, including some people who had not even been involved at all.<br /> <br /> In reality, there was only one person on the Scion forums who was terrible and intolerant, and I have not seen him on the forums since.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 09-12-2014, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T00:14:13-07:00","id":253896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253773#post253773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I remember that event quite differently, actually. Being one of the people Eldagusto decided to make personal attacks against in the &quot;secrecy&quot; of the Exalted forum when he was disagreed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember this incident differently, mostly because I spent some time PMing with Eldagusto and others after the incident, but since I didn't participate in that particular incident as I recall, it's not really relevant to the question.<br /> <br /> This thread actually displays some of the behaviour that at least I view as the reason this thread exists. The fact that mentioning of the marvel mythology actually had a light weight version of the response it would've gotten in another thread, is an indicator of that. I mean, the very verbal and active opposition to the thread start...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's with someone who people had at least heard of and had a modicrum respect on a topic that was at least created by White Wolf and therefore had a measure of credit if for no other reason than name attachment.<br /> <br /> Heaven forbid someone completely new come in and put forth ideas that don't have the same backing.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I saw what Rich was talking about, and I also knew where he was going. And yeah, that's my story. </div> </div> </div>I can sympathize with that. I've tried to make positive contributions and such on this forum only to be told that my contributions were &quot;horrible&quot; or flat out &quot;vulgar&quot;: If someone dislikes my ideas, fine, but derailing and shutting down entire threads for it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) Negative General: &quot;Your idea sucks&quot; </div> </div> </div>The thing is, I can live with that. I don't give 2 cents worth to general statements like that. If someone has something actual positive to add It's okay as long as it keeps the thread intent intact.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'd like to do x, any suggestions&quot;<br /> &quot;this is total YYY because of ZZZ&quot;<br /> &quot;Very well, I will keep that in mind, thank you&quot;<br /> <br /> Is a valid discussion and the issue has been mentioned and it doesn't need to derail the thread and undo any attempts at the original thread intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","user":"Gemstone","date":". 09-10-2014, 04:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T03:18:46-07:00","id":253933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253773#post253773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I remember that event quite differently, actually. Being one of the people Eldagusto decided to make personal attacks against in the &quot;secrecy&quot; of the Exalted forum when he was disagreed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>really </i>weren't any attacks against you. It was an Exalted thread about the Exalted community. It had nothing to do with you or the Scion community until you posted in the thread going on about how Eldagusto had, <i>somehow</i>, wronged you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even if he <i>had </i>actually attacked you, you should have just reported his post and let the mods handle it. The decision to <i>personally retaliate</i> is what turned that thread into a giant clusterfuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T04:11:35-07:00","id":253962,"title":"","content":"If anyone's intersted in a silver lining, here, it's that the Scion forum community is so passionate that this thread has blown out this large in so short a time. Ideas are being bandied back and forth. Examined, defined and then redefined. It's, honestly, what keeps me coming back to read more.<br /> <br /> It seems that this passion is perhaps at the core of the problems here. Because where a less passionate forum might just take someone's disagreed with idea and let it go, we're all arguing every little point. Not out of a desire to flame or troll anyone but because we want the game (everyone's game!) to be the very best it can be, and in that perhaps our passions get the better of us and sometimes some of us get too emotionally caught up in trying to show everyone else how awesome our idea is and get frustrated when people don't 'get it'. Because at the end of the day we all play the game for different reasons, and often with different game pantheons (either RAW, rules modded or out and out home-brewed) in mind.<br /> <br /> I don't really have a honking opinion about RichT's original post, or any real concern that the first time I disagree with someone I'm going to get spanked. I just mostly want to say how happy I am to share the forum with people who are so passionate about the game, the premise of the game and where the game can go that they get so riled up about things.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty confident in hoping that passion for the best the game can be will not be mistaken for personal attacks or bullying, but rather seen as spirited debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T09:35:56-07:00","id":254150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/252750-scion-fans-all-of-you?p=253933#post253933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>really </i>weren't any attacks against you. It was an Exalted thread about the Exalted community. It had nothing to do with you or the Scion community until you posted in the thread going on about how Eldagusto had, <i>somehow</i>, wronged you.<br /> <br /> Even if he <i>had </i>actually attacked you, you should have just reported his post and let the mods handle it. The decision to <i>personally retaliate</i> is what turned that thread into a giant clusterfuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eldagusto really did attack Telgar and several other people. His threads were reported, then the mods intervened and deleted large chunks of that thread, completely deleted another one of his threads, and banned him for a while. But we should get back on topic. Regardless of my earlier concerns, I think nothing but good can come from people stating their goals and intentions at the beginning of the post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 09-12-2014, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T17:33:44-07:00","id":254866,"title":"","content":"Have to say it doesn't seem terribly appropriate to dig into personal forum drama between a group of folks from awhile back. At the very least, the juicy details aren't necessary.<br /> <br /> Hope things have cooled down by the time second edition rolls out, I'm looking forward to discussing it. I feel like a number of posts in this thread have really overestimated just how easy it is to explain to people what they're doing is messed up and insensitive without getting hostile with them. I certainly get being <i>tired </i>of doing it (lord knows anyone who deals with this sort of thing regularly in real life can sympathize) but given that it's a forum and a textual medium which affords us the opportunity to compose our thoughts and then post them, it seems eminently reasonable for the mods to ask that we not assume the absolute worst about people or their ideas.<br /> <br /> If a dude is gonna be a dick about it, they'll make it clear when they respond to your civil discussion with the sort of unreasonable and hostile response that warrants moderation. Don't throw the first rock and all that. If whatever they said was bad enough that it really seems like they couldn't have anything less than hostile intent in posting whatever they posted, pass it on to the Mods, they'll do their job.<br /> <br /> And if it seems somewhere in between those two things, pass it on to the mods still. They'll check it out and act if they believe the rules are being violated. That's what they're here for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T12:48:28-07:00","id":256756,"title":"","content":"*Finally reads this threads OP and dies laughing* I love it, I am, as I type this, trying not to pee myself laughing at the collective faces of the Forums Trolls as they read this and realize that there is now a rule saying &quot;Don't be a fucking Troll&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T13:32:23-07:00","id":256799,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I haven't seen so much kerfuffle about a guy saying &quot;be cool to each other&quot; since the New Testament.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T16:30:17-07:00","id":256859,"title":"","content":"I know, it's not like he's saying &quot;Your not allowed to disagree with anyone ever about something&quot; just saying be constructive in the manner in which you respond and if all you can say is &quot;Your a stupid head&quot; than keep it to yourself, go have a juice box and have your mommy tuck you in for a nap like the juvenile man-child that you are&quot; <br /> <br /> Of course this is RP'ers we're talking about and I'm not to proud to say that on a rare occasion, I have turned into the big green horned forums monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the